From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:46:19 +0000
Subject: Update tzdata to 2026e

Brings ICU's time zone data up to tzdata 2026e, matching upstream ICU's
19dfb44a6 ("Update tzdata to 2026e"). Among other changes, 2026e maps
Europe/London and Europe/Dublin to the GMT metazone. With 2026d they map
only to the British and Irish metazones, which have no English winter
name, so after daylight saving time ends ICU formats their long time zone
name as "GMT+00:00" instead of "Greenwich Mean Time".

This applies on top of update_tzdata_to_2026d.patch and follows the same
approach: the source/data/misc text files are upstream's at 19dfb44a6, and
only the metaZones.res and zoneinfo64.res items of common/icudtl.dat are
replaced with upstream's, keeping every other item and the existing layout.
Making the same replacement in upstream 5aa52620, the parent of the tzdata
roll, reproduces upstream 19dfb44a6's common/icudtl.dat byte for byte.

This patch can be removed once Chromium's DEPS pins ICU at or after
19dfb44a6.

